      {
        "id": 231198,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-06-23T23:12:43.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I mean, to be fair, nearly every other celestial body in our solar system has its nomenclature derived from Greco-Roman mythology.&nbsp; It makes sense to refer to the Earth and the Moon in similarl linguistics.&nbsp; Besides, Moon/Luna is a moon.&nbsp; The idea of a moon, as a smaller body orbiting a planet, is a term unto itself, so it makes sense to have a name that would directly refer to Earth's Moon.</p>\n<p>Not disagreeing with you by any stretch, but I can see the other side as well.</p>",
