        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I mean, to be fair, nearly every other celestial body in our solar system has its nomenclature derived from Greco-Roman mythology.&nbsp; It makes sense to refer to the Earth and the Moon in similarl linguistics.&nbsp; Besides, Moon/Luna is a moon.&nbsp; The idea of a moon, as a smaller body orbiting a planet, is a term unto itself, so it makes sense to have a name that would directly refer to Earth's Moon.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Not disagreeing with you by any stretch, but I can see the other side as well.</p>",
