        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-11-21T15:50:20.564Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Oh man, Adam failed at Christianity so hard!  Aeon Girl is the wine, the Oblivaeon Shards are loaves of bread…obviously Progeny is the fishes!</p>\n<p>My biggest regret about this whole mostly-abandoned forum thing is that it didn’t involve the Playtest forums being opened up to everybody.  There’s so much info about what wound up on the cutting room floor, things like Scions and Missions from the early drafts of OblivAeon when he really had you fighting until ALL environments were destroyed, or VOTM decks for every character who didn’t end up getting one…I really want to know all the stuff they used to think they were going to publish someday, and as of now that’s not happening.  I wish I had the files.</p>\n<p>Anyway, obvious reason to have more scions - there are infinite other realities OA has to destroy, they have to have included creatures akin to Borr and Empyreon who are native to the Inversiverse and Extremiverse and Animalverse and so forth.</p>\n<p>The intangibility question really makes me think of when I say down with the D&amp;D Monster Manual and Savage Species, started trying to figure out monstrous characters with full adventuring gear, and one of the first ones I tackled was the Air Elemental.  I had to figure out how HP and damage and equipment all worked for that creature that was literally just made of air.</p>\n<p>I’m surprised that the Heir Apparent wasn’t the Hare Apparent, from the Animalverse.  Surely that happens at some point.</p>\n<p>“Dave’s not here, man!” IYKYK</p>\n<p>More peak comedy in the outro, not quite as good as Who’s on First, but comparably good and more original, so gets a bit more credit for that.</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
